      "message": "Hey Theodore! Thanks for pointing this out! You are right that the thread pool is being started twice, that\u0027s because `ABinderProcess_...` functions are C wrappers for methods of `android::ProcessState`. I suppose, you are talking about this check:\n\n```\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/native/libs/binder/ProcessState.cpp;l\u003d411;drc\u003db763b1493a1c54746cf5580cd7894474d987d4d1\n\nstatus_t ProcessState::setThreadPoolMaxThreadCount(size_t maxThreads) {\n    LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL_IF(mThreadPoolStarted \u0026\u0026 maxThreads \u003c mMaxThreads,\n           \"Binder threadpool cannot be shrunk after starting\");\n```        \n\nIt seems to me that it\u0027s not firing because it accesses `mThreadPoolStarted` w/o taking `mLock` and it gets a stale value.\n\nWhen reviewing this, I have missed the fact about the nature of `ABinderProcess_...`. I was supposing that we are starting thread pools for different Binder namespaces.",
